{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01KxngtLobEKVkYtUjs2r42h", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://pro.guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://cms.megaphone.fm/channel/NPTNI4549918435\"}, {\"url\": \"https://untappedcities.com/?p=465965\"}, {\"url\": \"https://untappedcities.com/richard-serras-first-major-outdoor-installation-was-located-at-183rd-street-in-the-bronx-nyc\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.singulart.com/blog/en/?p=134145\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.pressreader.com/usa/the-day/20240404/281784224111294\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/richard-serra-audio-biography--6134072\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.Britannica.com/summary/Richard-Serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.annexgalleries.com/artists/biography/2151\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:25:20.859Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Richard Serra first outdoor sculptures country", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01WemMGBohbZGRTtj6p5QqY7", "content": [{"title": "Serra, Richard", "url": "https://pro.guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra"}, {"title": "Serra, Richard", "url": "https://guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra"}, {"title": "Richard Serra - Audio Biography", "url": "https://cms.megaphone.fm/channel/NPTNI4549918435"}, {"title": "untappedcities.com", "url": "https://untappedcities.com/?p=465965"}, {"title": "richard serras first major outdoor installation was located at 183rd street in the bronx nyc", "url": "https://untappedcities.com/richard-serras-first-major-outdoor-installation-was-located-at-183rd-street-in-the-bronx-nyc"}, {"title": "Artists in the History", "url": "https://www.singulart.com/blog/en/?p=134145"}, {"title": "Richard Serra, sculptor of massive masterworks", "url": "https://www.pressreader.com/usa/the-day/20240404/281784224111294"}, {"title": "richard serra audio biography  6134072", "url": "https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/richard-serra-audio-biography--6134072"}, {"title": "Richard Serra", "url": "https://www.Britannica.com/summary/Richard-Serra"}, {"title": "Richard Serra Biography", "url": "https://www.annexgalleries.com/artists/biography/2151"}]}, "The first outdoor works were in the United States, but the sources disagree on which piece came first.\n\n- **Pulitzer Piece (St. Louis area, Missouri):** The Guggenheim Bilbao timeline credits this as his first site-specific work and the first of his large outdoor sculptures.\n- **To Encircle Base Plate Hexagram, Right Angles Inverted (1968 or 1970, New York):** An audio biography dates this 1968 work as his first large-scale outdoor sculpture. Untapped Cities places it in the Bronx at 183rd Street and Webster Avenue, and says the city permit was arranged in 1970 (the Park Administration told him that for $250, they would give him a permit to work on a street in the Bronx). The audio biography's claim that it was on a Long Island beach conflicts with this, and that podcast-style source looks less reliable.\n- **Shift (Ontario, Canada, 1970–72):** This is a later, well-known site-specific work, with six large concrete walls in a field in King City, Ontario.\n\nOverall, the best-supported answer is that Serra's first large outdoor works were made in the United States, with Pulitzer Piece cited by the Guggenheim as the first large outdoor sculpture. The Bronx piece is the most commonly described \"first major outdoor\" installation, and it is the one with the most detailed sourcing here. I did not find a source that settles the question definitively."], "durationSeconds": 6.319253916, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01KxngtLobEKVkYtUjs2r42h", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
