{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01D6GAYbDDQJoSgaP6Kr2nrd", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://untappedcities.com/?p=465965\"}, {\"url\": \"https://untappedcities.com/richard-serras-first-major-outdoor-installation-was-located-at-183rd-street-in-the-bronx-nyc\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/richard-serra-audio-biography--6134072\"}, {\"url\": \"https://readingoffice.com/?p=464\"}, {\"url\": \"https://readingoffice.com/richard-serra/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.britannica.com/print/article/1093333\"}, {\"url\": \"https://kids.kiddle.co/Richard_Serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://human.libretexts.org/Courses/Palo_Verde_College/Art_History%3A_Renaissance_to_Modern/10%3A_The_Transformation_of_the_Art_World_(1970-1999)/10.08%3A_Sculpture_(1970-2000)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://pro.guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://human.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Art/Art_History_and_Theory/A_World_Perspective_of_Art_History%3A_1400CE_to_the_21st_Century_(Gustlin_and_Gustlin)/07%3A_The_Transformation_of_the_Art_World_(1970-1999)/7.08%3A_Sculpture_(1970-2000)\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:25:31.969Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "\"Serra\" \"first outdoor\" sculpture Japan OR Netherlands OR Canada 1970", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01SjrCnyH3y6C5CzjAFxhiQo", "content": [{"title": "untappedcities.com", "url": "https://untappedcities.com/?p=465965"}, {"title": "richard serras first major outdoor installation was located at 183rd street in the bronx nyc", "url": "https://untappedcities.com/richard-serras-first-major-outdoor-installation-was-located-at-183rd-street-in-the-bronx-nyc"}, {"title": "richard serra audio biography  6134072", "url": "https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/richard-serra-audio-biography--6134072"}, {"title": "Richard Serra", "url": "https://readingoffice.com/?p=464"}, {"title": "Richard Serra", "url": "https://readingoffice.com/richard-serra/"}, {"title": "Richard Serra", "url": "https://www.britannica.com/print/article/1093333"}, {"title": "kids encyclopedia robot", "url": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Richard_Serra"}, {"title": "10.08%3A Sculpture (1970 2000)", "url": "https://human.libretexts.org/Courses/Palo_Verde_College/Art_History%3A_Renaissance_to_Modern/10%3A_The_Transformation_of_the_Art_World_(1970-1999)/10.08%3A_Sculpture_(1970-2000)"}, {"title": "Serra, Richard", "url": "https://pro.guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra"}, {"title": "7.08%3A Sculpture (1970 2000)", "url": "https://human.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Art/Art_History_and_Theory/A_World_Perspective_of_Art_History%3A_1400CE_to_the_21st_Century_(Gustlin_and_Gustlin)/07%3A_The_Transformation_of_the_Art_World_(1970-1999)/7.08%3A_Sculpture_(1970-2000)"}]}, "The search points to a 1970 Japan installation as Serra's first outdoor work, with the Bronx piece usually cited as his first major outdoor installation in New York. Sources disagree on the details, so treat these as leads rather than settled facts.\n\n- **Japan (1970), the strongest candidate for \"first outdoor\":** One account says his first outdoor sculptures, *To Encircle Base Plate (Hexagram)* and *Sugi Tree* (both 1970), were placed in Ueno Park for the Tokyo Biennale as part of the \"Tokyo Biennale.\" A Guggenheim chronology also notes that he traveled to Japan with Joan Jonas, took part in the Tokyo Biennial, and encountered Kyoto's Zen gardens Travels to Japan with Joan Jonas; participates in the Tokyo Biennial and discovers the Zen gardens of Kyoto.\n- **United States (1970):** Several sources describe the Bronx piece, *To Encircle Base Plate Hexagon, Right Angles Inverted*, as his first large outdoor work. One says the idea was first developed in Ueno Park and that the Bronx version was 26 feet in diameter, made of sheet metal circle, and embedded in the surface of the street. The site was on 183rd Street in the Bronx.\n- **Canada (1970–72):** *Shift* is a site-specific work described as six large concrete walls, each measuring 60 feet long and 10 feet high, that are arranged in a zigzag pattern across a field in King City, Ontario, Canada. This source gives the dates 1970–72, but it is a less reliable audio-biography page.\n- **Netherlands:** The results did not mention a Dutch outdoor work from 1970. The Maastricht piece *Hours of the Day* appears only as a 1990 work, so it is not relevant to the 1970 question.\n\n**Conflicts:** One audio-biography page says the 1968 *To Encircle* was on a Long Island beach. That contradicts the other sources, which place it in the Bronx in 1970, so I would discount it. The Guggenheim timeline credits *Pulitzer Piece: Stepped Elevation* near St. Louis as his first large outdoor sculpture, but the result gives no date, so I could not confirm its timing."], "durationSeconds": 8.668147458, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01D6GAYbDDQJoSgaP6Kr2nrd", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
